{
  "name": "What to Do When Your Drywall Gets Storm Damaged",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "When a storm hits and leaves your drywall wet, it can feel overwhelming, but tackling it quickly is key. First things first, document the damage with photos for insurance purposes. Next, you absolutely need to identify and stop the water source to prevent further issues. Once the water is contained, remove any baseboards or compromised drywall that's clearly beyond saving. Getting airflow to the cavity is crucial, so bring in fans and dehumidifiers. Don't forget to remove any wet insulation behind the wall; it’s a breeding ground for problems. After everything is thoroughly dry, you can install new drywall, tape, finish, and repaint. Sometimes, knowing when to call in the experts can save you a lot of headache and cost in the long run, especially if you're dealing with extensive damage or suspect hidden issues.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
